<title>HONG KONG: Top shareholder cuts Founder HK stake.</title>
<headline>Top shareholder cuts Founder HK stake.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Controlling shareholder Peking University Founder Group Corp has cut its stake in Founder (Hong Kong) Ltd by 25 million shares, or five percent of the company's share capital, the Hong Kong stock exchange said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It gave no details on the current shareholding of Peking University Founder in the computer software maker.</p>
<p>The China state-owned enterprise Peking University Founder held 55.6 percent of Founder (Hong Kong) as at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>Shares of Founder (Hong Kong) rose HK$0.125 or 3.85 percent to HK$3.375 in Wednesday morning trade.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
